# =============================================================================
# Build context for the images (Dockerfile).
# =============================================================================
# The `loader` stage is fully self-contained: it apt-installs pgloader + the psql
# client and inlines its load script via a Dockerfile heredoc. It COPYs NOTHING
# from the tree. Every other stage needs source from packages/ -- the three wheels
# that merge into the one PEP 420 `file_analyzer` namespace:
#   * `wheels`                  -> builds file-analyzer-{client,server,engine}
#                                  wheels from packages/{client,server,engine}
#                                  (the server/engine setup.py shims read the
#                                  version from packages/client, so all three
#                                  trees travel together).
#   * `go-build`/`reader`       -> the Go VIEW-reader under
#                                  packages/engine/file_analyzer/views/go.
#   * `engine`/`monitor`/`mcp`  -> install the client + engine wheels.
#   * `server`                  -> installs the client + server wheels.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-include packages/ alone. This keeps the context
# to just what the source-using stages build.
*

!packages/**

# Never bring caches, local build outputs or prebuilt Go binaries into the
# context -- the images build their own (a stale host binary built for another
# OS/arch would otherwise shadow the in-image `go build`).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
packages/*/build/
packages/*/dist/
packages/*/*.egg-info/
packages/**/go/*.exe
packages/client/file_analyzer/client/go/client-reader
packages/engine/file_analyzer/views/go/repo-reader
packages/engine/file_analyzer/core/go/repo-injector
packages/engine/file_analyzer/router/go/analysis-plane
packages/engine/file_analyzer/monitor/go/monitor-pool
packages/server/file_analyzer/server/go/backup-pool

# (The AnalysisEngine artifacts and every server database/backup/shard are NOT
#  baked into any image -- they are mounted at runtime by docker-compose.yml:
#  /artifacts (loader/reader/engine/monitor), /workspace (the source repo), and
#  the server's /data + /shards/* named volumes.)
